&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;As a Senior Finance &amp;amp; Strategy Manager on the Core FP&amp;amp;A team, you&#39;ll provide CFO-level financial partnership to critical support functions across Coinbase, including People, Legal, Compliance, Policy, and Finance. This team sits at the center of company-wide resource allocation, investment strategy, and long-term financial planning. You&#39;ll partner directly with multiple C-level executives and their leadership teams to shape how Coinbase deploys capital and scales its operations, while leading and developing a team of finance professionals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the financial health of multiple major functional areas, serving as the primary finance partner to 3+ C-level executives and their leadership teams on resource allocation, investment strategy, and long-term planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the vision for how Finance partners with the business by identifying and implementing new analytical frameworks, efficiency opportunities, and operational improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of finance professionals, setting clear performance expectations and building a culture of strategic thinking and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with People, Legal, Compliance, Policy, and Finance leadership to align on budgets, forecasts, headcount planning, and strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape company-wide investment decisions by building financial models, scenario analyses, and business cases that inform executive decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute regular financial reporting and variance analysis, translating complex data into actionable insights for senior leadership and the CFO&#39;s office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in FP&amp;amp;A, strategic finance, or a combination of these roles (investment banking experience counts), with a significant portion spent in leadership roles at high-growth technology companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2 years of direct people management experience, with a track record of coaching and developing finance professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success as a strategic partner to C-level executives, with specific examples of influencing company-level strategy, resource allocation, or investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build, maintain, and present complex financial models that drive executive decision-making across multiple functional areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
