&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manager, Corporate Programs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Corporate &amp;amp; Strategic Programs (CSP) sits within Coinbase&#39;s central Business org, leveraging program management to supercharge execution on the company&#39;s most critical priorities. As a Manager, Corporate Programs, you&#39;ll own two of our most visible cross-functional programs: CORA (Change Oversight &amp;amp; Risk Assessment), which mitigates risk across all product launches and system changes, and Planning, which manages Executive QBRs, OKRs, and dependencies management. You&#39;ll drive both programs end-to-end, translating complex process challenges into scalable solutions with direct visibility to senior leadership.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct research and analysis to understand internal customer pain points and create solutions prioritized into a clear roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Executive QBR planning cycles end-to-end, from company guidance through to final outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain CORA&#39;s operating rhythms including weekly and monthly reporting, and represent CORA during audits and compliance exams with internal and external stakeholders including regulators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with technical teams (IT, data, engineering) when solutions require more complex technical builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain all enablement resources including guidance, policies, procedures, FAQs, training materials, and AI agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement scalable solutions to systemic process and tooling challenges across both programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in product operations or program management for software/product initiatives, with experience owning cross-functional programs end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to turn ambiguous or conflicting inputs into clear, actionable plans and drive them to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with technical teams and translating business requirements into tooling or process solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Atlassian suite (Jira, Confluence) and experience leveraging AI to automate and accelerate workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication with the ability to facilitate senior stakeholder dialogues and drive toward outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position ID:&lt;/strong&gt; P77647&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;LinkedIn: #LI-Remote&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Base salary varies by location (see range below). Total compensation may also include equity and bonus eligibility, and benefits (medical, dental, vision, 401(k)).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
